        "h": 7
      },
      "content": "<div style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: var(--text-color, #333); background-color: var(--bg-color, #fafafa); padding: 12px; line-height: 1.6;\">\n    \n    <p><h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac);\">What this table shows:</h4>\n    This table lists test case counts for various <span style=\"color: var(--highlight-color, #81c784); font-weight:bold;\">functional areas</span> within the application, broken down by execution type (manual or automated) and associated execution status. Each row represents a specific functional area.</p>\n    \n    <p><h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac);\">Why it matters:</h4>\n    It provides visibility into how testing efforts are distributed across different parts of the application. This present the team functional area expertises and helps ensure that all critical areas receive adequate coverage during regression and hardening phases.</p>\n    \n    <p><h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac);\">How to interpret:</h4>\n    Since we follow a <span style=\"color: var(--warning-color, #ffb74d); font-weight:bold;\">risk-based testing approach</span>, different functional areas may have varying levels of risk impact. While generally, a high-risk area might have more automated tests for faster feedback, it is still possible that some complex areas may still require manual checks.</p>\n</div>",
      "mode": "html"
    },
