      "content": "<div style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: var(--text-color, #333); background-color: var(--bg-color, #fafafa); padding: 12px; line-height: 1.6;\">\n    \n    <p><h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac);\">What this table shows:</h4>\n    This table lists test case counts for various <span style=\"color: var(--highlight-color, #81c784); font-weight:bold;\">labels</span> within the application, broken down by execution type (manual or automated) and associated execution status. Each row represents a specific area.</p>\n    \n    <p><h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac);\">Why it matters:</h4>\n    We are using for a various reasons and this table provides visibility into how testing efforts are distributed across them. This helps ensure that wehave enough visibility during regression and hardening phases.</p>\n    \n    <p><h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac);\">How to interpret:</h4>\n    Since we follow a <span style=\"color: var(--warning-color, #ffb74d); font-weight:bold;\">risk-based testing approach</span>, different labels may have varying levels of risk impact and different meaning so only those who knows what the specific label means can speak on the value of visibility for it</p>\n    \n</div>",
